# ORIGINS — mandatory safety rules

This repository is the canonical project source. Preserve working material and make incremental changes.

## Never do these without explicit user approval
- Do not delete existing files or folders.
- Do not rename or move existing files or folders.
- Do not replace an existing subsystem with a new architecture just because it seems cleaner.
- Do not rewrite unrelated files while implementing a task.
- Do not discard existing assets, manifests, source references, docs, or tools.
- Do not merge visual themes or asset families.
- Do not copy legacy ORIGINS/GameInter/chat-upload material into the new implementation unless explicitly requested.
- Do not force-push or rewrite Git history.

## Required working method
1. Read `CURSOR_START_HERE.md` and `docs/GAME_ARCHITECTURE_V1.md` before significant work.
2. Inspect the current tree before editing.
3. Reuse existing modules and paths when they already satisfy the architecture.
4. Add new files in their assigned folder instead of creating parallel duplicate systems.
5. Touch the smallest possible set of files for each task.
6. Keep changes incremental and reversible.
7. Use small, descriptive commits. One logical change per commit when practical.
8. Before a destructive operation, stop and ask for approval.
9. When a task is complete, report files created/modified and explicitly state that no unrelated files were removed.

## Preservation rule
If an existing file appears obsolete but is not blocking the requested task, leave it in place and document it for later review. Never remove it opportunistically.

## Source-of-truth rule
When documentation and code disagree, do not silently choose one. Report the conflict and preserve both until the project owner decides.
